From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no Google account check (ListAccounts)

Chrome's Google sign-in kept asking accounts.google.com which Google
accounts the browser's cookies belong to (gaia_auth_list_accounts): at
startup for AI Mode (0085 turned that off) and whenever a google.com
cookie was deleted, which at the sign-in screen happened every few
minutes. NickelOS has no Google accounts (local accounts, and Google
closed sign-in and sync to builds other than its own), so the answer is
always none: GaiaCookieManagerService::TriggerListAccounts() gives it
(the cookie jar's accounts are fresh and empty) without asking.

Signing in to Google's websites is not affected: their cookies work as
before; only Chrome's own idea of the signed-in accounts stays empty.

diff --git a/components/signin/internal/identity_manager/gaia_cookie_manager_service.cc b/components/signin/internal/identity_manager/gaia_cookie_manager_service.cc
index 92b485477138b..997fc3646cd3f 100644
--- a/components/signin/internal/identity_manager/gaia_cookie_manager_service.cc
+++ b/components/signin/internal/identity_manager/gaia_cookie_manager_service.cc
@@ -527,21 +527,11 @@ GaiaCookieManagerService::GetCachedListAccounts() {
 }
 
 void GaiaCookieManagerService::TriggerListAccounts() {
-  // Callers suspect that a check to Gaia needs to be done, don't rely on the
-  // in progress request, conditions might have changed while the request is
-  // in-flight.
-  // Note: /ListAccounts requests is optimized in `OptimizeListAccounts()`
-  // called in `HandleNextRequest()`. Only if there are no other requests in the
-  // queue that `HandleNextRequest()` won't be called before executing
-  // /ListAccounts.
-  requests_.push_back(GaiaCookieRequest::CreateListAccountsRequest());
-  if (requests_.size() == 1) {
-    fetcher_retries_ = 0;
-    listAccountsUnexpectedServerResponseRetried_ = false;
-    signin_client_->DelayNetworkCall(base::BindOnce(
-        &GaiaCookieManagerService::MaybeStartFetchingListAccounts,
-        weak_ptr_factory_.GetWeakPtr()));
-  }
+  // NickelOS: no Google accounts, ever (local accounts; Google closed sign-in
+  // and sync to other builds): the answer is always "none", so it is given
+  // here instead of asking accounts.google.com, which Chrome did whenever a
+  // google.com cookie went (at the sign-in screen, every few minutes).
+  list_accounts_stale_ = false;
 }
 
 void GaiaCookieManagerService::TriggerListAccountsIfStale() {
